  "description": "Nuri hasn’t changed much since she was in elementary school. She still has a temper, she still lives in the same house, and she’s still tragically short. Her childhood friend Homil, however, has changed a lot. Several years after he moved away, Homil returns as Nuri’s neighbor and high school classmate. Now, he’s not quite the same boy Nuri used to know. Sure, he’s still an idiot and a good friend, but something feels different, and Nuri is all too aware of it in a more-than-friendly way. She might not be growing any taller, but maybe some weird feelings about Homil are growing inside of her…\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)",
